# The toolchain the mips benchmarks and the codegen audit run inside.
#
# Both scripts publish numbers that are properties of what a compiler emits:
# bench/results-insn.csv counts executed instructions, and
# bench/notes-mips.md asserts the multiply lowering poly1305 and p256 get.
# An unpinned base image made those numbers move without a source change,
# which is the same drift CI hit when CLANG_RV resolved to whatever clang
# the runner shipped. CLAUDE.md requires the pin.
#
# The digest pins the base image exactly. It does not pin apk, which
# resolves against the live repository, so the scripts also assert the
# compiler's major version and print its full version beside the results.
# Bump both together, and re-measure in the same commit.
ALPINE_DIGEST=sha256:28bd5fe8b56d1bd048e5babf5b10710ebe0bae67db86916198a6eec434943f8b
CLANG_MAJOR=22
